{% extends "base.html.jinja" %}
{% from "_macros.html.jinja" import advisory_table %}
{% block content %}
<h1>Toxic algae advisories at {{ "California and Missouri" if "MO" in states_present else "California" }} lakes and rivers</h1>
<p class="lede">
  Which waters have a harmful algal bloom advisory on file with the state,
  when it was posted, and whether the state has recorded an end. For anyone
  heading to the water: swimmers, families, paddlers, anglers and dog owners.
</p>
<p class="muted">
  {% for f in source_files %}{% if f.source == "ca-swrcb-fhab" %}California: the state's file dated {{ f.file_date|date }}{% if f.newest_record_date %}, newest record {{ f.newest_record_date|date }}{% endif %}.{% elif f.source == "mo-dnr-hab" %} Missouri: read {{ f.fetched_at[:10]|date }}{% if f.newest_record_date %}, newest record {{ f.newest_record_date|date }}{% endif %}.{% endif %}{% endfor %}
  An advisory stays listed until the state records an end. A water that is
  not listed has no advisory on file, which is not the same as being free of algae.
</p>

<h2>Advisories posted in the last {{ recent_days }} days</h2>
{% if recent %}
{{ advisory_table(recent, root, "Advisories posted in the last " ~ recent_days ~ " days, newest first") }}
{% else %}
<p>The state's file has no advisory posted in the last {{ recent_days }} days. Older advisories with no all-clear recorded are listed on the next page.</p>
{% endif %}
<p><a href="{{ root }}advisories/">See all {{ recent|length + older_count }} waters whose latest record is an advisory</a>, including {{ older_count }} older ones the state never recorded an end for.</p>

<h2>Bringing a dog?</h2>
<p>Dogs swim through scum and drink lake water, so algae affects them more than most people. <a href="{{ root }}dogs/">How to read an advisory before a lake day with your dog</a>.</p>

<h2>Where else to check</h2>
<p>No single page covers every lake. <a href="{{ root }}where-to-check/">Where to check a California algae advisory</a> is a dated list of the state, county, park district and lake pages people use, and what each covers and does not.</p>

<h2>Find a lake</h2>
<p>{{ water_count }} lakes and rivers, each with its own page and every state record on file:</p>
<ul>
  <li><a href="{{ root }}county/">California, by county</a> (records since 2016)</li>
  {% if "MO" in states_present %}<li><a href="{{ root }}state/mo/">Missouri</a> (records since 2017)</li>{% endif %}
</ul>
{% endblock %}
